  "notes": [
    "uh_ubus_allowed requires session.access scope=ubus object=file function=exec (uhttpd omits scope). rpcd-mod-file then checks file.exec of the canonicalized executable first, then the cmdline.",
    "Bounded to fs.exec callers at luci b2e0be4b: iptables.js handleCounterReset iptables/ip6tables -Z, routes.js /sbin/ip -[46] neigh/route/rule, routesj.js /sbin/ip -[46] -j neigh/route/rule.",
    "Inventoried luci-ssl ACLs grant those cmdlines, not the bare executables. Extra tokens therefore miss.",
    "Missing SID is JSON-RPC ERROR_PARSE, not the all-zero sentinel.",
    "Unauthenticated is ERROR_ACCESS at uh_ubus_allowed. A ubus file.exec grant without the matching file ACL is UBUS_STATUS_PERMISSION_DENIED.",
    "Root list read/write '*' is stock rpcd.config, not a violation (expectation_id root-administration).",
    "Do not emit dispatcher, authorization_violation, path_found, luci object grants, or execv.",
    "shellquote and basename are not sanitizers. rpc_canonicalize_path is not a taint sanitizer.",
    "cgi-io cgi-exec listing of iptables stays on policy:cgi-exec-status-v1.",
    "luci-mod-network diagnostics/ifup and luci-mod-status-processes /bin/kill are not this slice."
  ],
